# {{projectName}}

MCP TypeScript SDK 2.0 client starter{{#if (and (includes transports 'stdio') (includes transports 'streamable'))}} for stdio and Streamable HTTP{{else if (includes transports 'stdio')}} for stdio{{else}} for Streamable HTTP{{/if}}.

The demo runs one complete workflow against the paired server:

1. Discover Tools, Resources, and Prompts.
2. Call `search_documents`.
3. Read the selected `kb://documents/{documentId}` Resource.
4. Get `review_document` with the selected document ID.

{{#if (includes transports 'stdio')}}By default, the stdio example starts `@my-mcp-hub/node-mcp-server`.{{/if}}{{#if (includes transports 'streamable')}} The HTTP example connects
to `http://localhost:8401/mcp`; set `MCP_SERVER_URL` to use another HTTP endpoint.{{/if}}{{#if (includes transports 'stdio')}}
Pass `StdioDemoOptions` to `runStdioDemo` to use another executable.{{/if}}

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

The test suite expects the paired server project in `../mcp-server-starter` and verifies the same workflow over the configured transports:

```bash
npm test
npm run build
```
